* =====================================================================================================
* usb_input__bq25180_in.lib  -  BQ25180 IN pin (input port only), base board U1 ball A2
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Part      : Texas Instruments BQ25180YBGR
* Datasheet : SLUSE99C (September 2021, revised January 2023), https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/bq25180.pdf
* Vendor model: no TI SPICE/PSpice model of the BQ25180 was found, so this is a behavioural model of
*             what the USB input network sees at IN.
*
* Modelled:
*   IQ_IN    input quiescent current 0.75 mA typ / 1 mA max at VIN = 5 V (Table 7.5)   -> param iq
*            drawn only above VIN_UVLOZ (exit UVLO, 3.0 V max, Table 7.5)
*   IIN      current through the input FET to SYS/BAT once the power path is up       -> param iin
*            (a constant-current sink = the ILIM loop; ILIM 500 mA setting 450..498 mA,
*            1050 mA setting 995..1100 mA, IIN max 1.1 A: Tables 7.1 / 7.4 / 7.5).  The tests use
*            iin = 0 for plug-in transients: the input FET is still off while the device qualifies
*            the source, and no load is the least-damped (worst) case for ringing.
*   ESD      ASSUMED pin clamp from GND (negative excursions): generic diode, RS = resd (default 3 ohm,
*            typical TLP slope of an HBM-2 kV-class on-chip clamp). TI does not specify the structure;
*            the tests compare the current through it with the HBM rating (Table 7.2, +-2500 V).
* NOT modelled: VIN_OVP (5.5/5.7/5.9 V, Table 7.5) and VINDPM loops, input-FET soft start, SYS/BAT
*   side, the positive-going internal clamp (IN is rated 25 V, Table 7.1; the tests compare the IN
*   node voltage with that), pin capacitance (negligible next to C1).
* Port naming: the ground port is called VSS, not GND: ngspice treats a node named 'gnd' as global ground
*   even inside a subcircuit, which would tie the pin to 0 whatever the netlist connects it to
*   (verifier fix 2026-10-19; it hid every wrong-connection fault on this pin).
* Pins: IN, GND
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt USBIN_BQ25180_IN IN VSS params: iq=0.75m iin=0 resd=3
* smooth enable above UVLO (3.0 V), ~50 mV wide, so DC sweeps stay continuous
Bin IN VSS I=(iq+iin)*0.5*(1+tanh((v(IN,VSS)-3.0)/0.05))
Rleak IN VSS 10Meg
* Vesd: 0 V probe, i(v.x<inst>.vesd) = current through the assumed clamp (positive = conducting)
Vesd VSS esda 0
Desd esda IN USBIN_BQ_ESD
.model USBIN_BQ_ESD D(IS=1e-15 N=1 RS={resd} CJO=0)
.ends USBIN_BQ25180_IN
